# Source: Ventrax AV4 report. Acceptance specification; execution is verified separately.
Feature: IAM account activation and delegated access

  Scenario: Activate password after verified initial payment
    Given Billing has confirmed an initial purchase and IAM has a pending account
    When the user provides a valid unused activation token and a valid password
    Then IAM stores an adaptive password hash and activates the account

  Scenario: Reject activation without a confirmed payment
    Given the initial purchase has not been confirmed by Billing
    When account activation is requested
    Then IAM does not activate the account

  Scenario: Sign in with email and password
    Given the user account is active and has a password
    When the user submits valid credentials
    Then IAM issues a session JWT without sending a recurring sign-in email

  Scenario: Reject invalid credentials
    Given an active account exists
    When an incorrect password is submitted
    Then IAM rejects authentication without disclosing account details

  Scenario: Reset the password with a one-time token
    Given the user has a valid unused recovery token
    When a new valid password is submitted
    Then IAM updates the password hash and invalidates the token

  Scenario: Deny a delegated action without the required permission
    Given the subuser has VIEW_CONSUMPTION on meter A and VIEW_ALERTS on meter B
    When the subuser requests VIEW_CONSUMPTION on meter B
    Then the requested backend operation is denied after checking the current meter-specific grants without exposing meter B consumption

  Scenario: Revoke a permission independently on each meter
    Given the subuser has VIEW_CONSUMPTION on meter A and VIEW_ALERTS on meter B
    When the primary user revokes VIEW_CONSUMPTION on meter A
    Then the subuser cannot view consumption on meter A
    And the subuser can still view alerts on meter B

  Scenario: Prevent subusers from accessing financial functions
    Given an authenticated subuser has delegated access to one meter
    When the subuser requests payment, subscription, or subuser administration
    Then the backend service denies the protected operation
